{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-002", "approach": "HYBRID+intact", "approach_base": "HYBRID", "flags": {"intact": true}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Douglass learned to read in Baltimore when Mrs. Auld kindly began teaching him the A, B, C and helped him spell words of three or four letters (Chapter VI). Mr. Auld found out and at once forbade her to continue, saying it was unlawful as well as unsafe to teach a slave to read, that learning would spoil the best slave and forever unfit him to be a slave, and that a slave should know nothing but to obey his master (Chapter VI). Douglass nevertheless finished learning to read and write in Baltimore with the assistance of his master's wife, as noted in the introductory biography of Frederick Douglass.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 1011 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o011", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b109", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [76319, 77330], "meta": {"chunk": 5734, "completed": 14, "prefix": 0}}, {"text": "[stripped: 650 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o015", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b197", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b198"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [173593, 174243], "meta": {"chunk": 5877, "completed": 39, "prefix": 0}}, {"text": "[stripped: 886 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o005", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b50"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [25277, 26163], "meta": {"chunk": 5656, "completed": 0, "prefix": 0}}, {"text": "[stri